WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.235
[Caroline] "Share Your World"

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.269
invites you to learn

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.404
about different cultures

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.839
through our personal stories.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:07.974
In this episode,

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.476
we're celebrating holidays

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.144
from our cultural backgrounds.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.220
[Caroline] Every culture has
its own holiday traditions.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.490
Today, we're sharing a
few of our favorites.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.325
There's a holiday in the Armenian culture

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.826
called Vartavar

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.328
or Vardavar,

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.997
depending on if you're an Eastern Armenian

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:32.432
or Western Armenian dialect.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:36.603
This usually happens in July,
and basically it is the day

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:40.273
where everyone splashes
each other with water.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.442
Everyone's running into fountains.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.879
It is just a countrywide water fight.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.248
Vardavar goes back to the Pagan times,

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:50.850
and it is to worship the goddess, Astghik,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.519
which is the goddess of water,

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:55.021
love, fertility, and beauty.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.524
And next summer, I am definitely

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:00.660
hoping I can go to Armenia

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.227
and stay at the

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.930
Armenia Marriott Hotel Yerevan.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.900
And if I can be there, during Vardavar,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.571
during the water fight of the year,

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.472
then that would be perfect,

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.374
because I can just walk out of my hotel

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:17.811
and there's the fountain
and I can get drenched,

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:20.747
and then just walk right back
into the hotel and carry on.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.015
[Debby] My favorite holiday,

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.017
for sure, is Christmas,

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:28.221
and I think more so because I'm not home.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.323
I live in LA and I'm not in Switzerland.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.592
So Christmas is usually
the time of the year

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.094
where I try to go home.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.830
What helps me, even more, to
get into the Christmas spirit

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.499
is our Christmas Market in Basel.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.367
Just walking through the market,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.704
you smell all the different
smells from the foods

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.940
and the drinks, and we
obviously have mulled wine,

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.541
which I think is kind of known here

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.710
or it's starting to get to be known here,

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.480
which is a hot wine with
different spices, with cinnamon,

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.081
and you can throw apples into it.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.750
I used to go every year
as a child and as a teen,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.620
so it's not that it's new every year.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.455
It's always the same,
usually the same people,

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:05.525
the same vendors, but
it's still always magical.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.427
It just is. I absolutely love it.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:10.196
[Caroline] Debby, will you
pick fondue or raclette

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.498
when you're at the market?

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:14.667
[Debby] Oh my gosh, I
get this question a lot.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:15.735
I think fondue.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.805
So they're both very interactive,

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.908
with the people that are sitting
around the table, you chat,

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.711
you talk, you exchange the
food that's on the table

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.714
that goes with it, like potatoes or corn

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.582
or whatever sides that you like.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.850
It's a really good dinner.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:33.520
I can't wait to go back home

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.457
and have a traditional
Swiss raclette or fondue.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:40.059
[Katrina] In my family, I think the holiday

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.295
that we look forward to the most

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.963
is always Thanksgiving,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.698
which is not, by any means,

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.368
a traditional Nigerian holiday,

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:52.438
but we've definitely made
it into our own version

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.306
of the holiday.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:57.177
For our Thanksgiving spread,
we have your typical turkey

00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:01.047
and your ham and your stuffing,
but we'll also throw in

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.983
a lot of traditional Nigerian dishes,

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:07.554
so we'll have jollof rice,
which is a staple in our food.

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:08.621
We'll have moi moi.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.291
Moi moi is black-eyed peas

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:16.596
that is blended with different
spices, like garlic, tomato,

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:19.132
a whole bunch of things,
and then it's boiled

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:22.001
into a bean round.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:22.969
It's really good.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.370
We'll have efo riro.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:28.808
Efo riro is a spinach stew,
that is my favorite stew,

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.945
typically eaten with a fufu of some type,

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:36.049
whether it's pounded yam or amala.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:39.752
You choose your fufu, but,
yeah, it's an American tradition

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.054
that we've made our own.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.689
[Jason] My favorite holiday

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:43.957
is Cambodian New Year.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:48.528
It happens the weekend of
April 13th, around that time,

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.730
and it's a lot of family time,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.165
and there's a lot of culture time.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:55.068
There's a little gambling as well.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:58.938
We call it Klah Klok, where
it's basically this sheet

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.573
that has different animals on it.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:03.509
We have dice, where we
put three dice in a bowl,

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:05.144
we shake it and people would

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:07.947
put dollars on the chicken

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:09.482
or on the crab,

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.450
and the dice would come out,

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.286
and if it has a chicken or
a crab, you get a dollar

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.420
for each of the things.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.557
[Caroline] Jason, do you bet
on any particular animal?

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.994
Is one luckier than the other?

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:21.995
[Jason] I just love crab.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.196
I think it's lucky,

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:26.466
so I would definitely,
always try to bet on crab.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.868
[Caroline] I'm glad we
can virtually connect,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:33.273
because sometimes it feels
like you're just here,

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:36.075
and you can't travel and
stuff, but I honestly feel like

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:39.779
I went to new locations,
just by chatting with you,

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:43.616
so I traveled in my chair.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:44.384
[Debby] I love that.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.553
[Jason] Yeah, it's definitely
great to be able to connect.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.589
Sometimes we feel like
we're different people,

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.591
but food brings people together.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:55.561
You feel that connection
over our love for food.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:58.765
[Caroline] I think we can
all agree that we can't wait

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:01.734
to come back together and
travel when we're able.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.203
We hope you're excited to
some day experience these

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:07.240
and other holiday traditions
in their home countries.

